<p>A puzzle by Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon, from the <a href="https://archive.org/details/Games-Magazine-October-1991-images/page/n61/mode/2up">October 1991 issue</a> of <em>Games</em> magazine:</p>
<p>You&#8217;re visiting a familiar island on which each resident either invariably lies or invariably tells the truth. Three residents appear.</p>
<p>Resident 1: We&#8217;re all liars.<br />
Resident 2: Just one of us is a truth teller.</p>
<p>The third resident doesn&#8217;t speak. Which of the three are telling the truth?</p>

